  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, and `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` passes: 47 passed, 2 skipped. I didn't check whether those two skips come from my tests; I assumed they were already there.\n\n- **Class:** `KeyValue` is a `ParamType` subclass in `src/click/types.py`, placed right after `UUIDParameterType`. It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=`, or with an empty key, fails through `self.fail(...)` with `'...' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Export:** `src/click/__init__.py` exports the class itself, not an instance.\n- **Tests:** I added two tests to `tests/test_types.py`. One covers valid input (`a=b`, `a=b=c`, `a=`). The other covers `abc`, `=value` and the empty string, checking for exit code 2 and the error message.\n\nI also made `convert()` pass an existing tuple through unchanged. That wasn't in your spec, so say if you'd rather it didn't.",
